# Ownership of the template, and the allowlist the onboarding automation reads.
#
# `onboard-customer.sh` requires the actor to appear here *and* to hold write
# access to this repository before it will create a repository or open a
# Terraform pull request. Two checks rather than one, because they fail
# differently: repository access is revoked when someone leaves, and this file
# is what a reviewer reads to answer "who can do this".
#
# Handles, not teams, on purpose. Resolving team membership from Actions needs
# the App to hold organisation `Members: read`, and adding a permission whose
# only job is to check a permission is a poor trade for a list this short.

* @acrois

# Changing the onboarding automation must require the same trust as running it.
/.github/CODEOWNERS               @acrois
/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/          @acrois
/.github/scripts/                 @acrois
/.github/workflows/               @acrois
